 The executor runs each test on the defense's gem5 prototype and uses the simulator's white-box access to steer it toward its target execution using directives (\S\ref{sec:speculation-directives}): it forces branch predictions and holds branch resolution, leaving the defense's own logic unchanged (\S\ref{sec:discussion}). Its \emph{Inspector} flags a run as a hit if the target execution's transmitter transmits, by the defense's transmission criterion, while the target execution's speculation conditions still hold (which branches are unresolved and which instructions are uncommitted). It reads these events directly from gem5's trace, so detection needs no attacker, probe program, or second run (\S\ref{sec:transmission-requirement}).
 
